    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `triage` in `app/worker.py`. The test suite passes (2 tests), but both tests are for `ask_with_limits`, so nothing exercises `triage` yet and I haven't run it against the API.\n\nIt sends one request per ticket with the same model, system prompt and `max_tokens=512` as `ask_with_limits`. The answer, `tokens_remaining` and `request_id` all come from that one response, the same way the sync version gets them. `throttle` is `True` when `tokens_remaining` is below `LOW_WATERMARK` (2,000), otherwise `False`.\n\nThis isn't a straight copy of the sync code with `await` added. In the installed anthropic 1.8.0, `raw.parse()` on the async client also has to be awaited. Without that, `message` would be a coroutine and building the answer would fail. I await both the `create(...)` call and `parse()`, and read the headers directly because they aren't async.\n\nLike `ask_with_limits`, it raises a `KeyError` if a response is missing the `anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining` header. If you'd rather the worker handle that case some other way, such as treating a missing header as \"throttle\", say so and I'll add it. I can also add a test for `triage` that fakes the async raw response."
  },
